  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "The spec does the real association: it stubs the batched /pulls read with an open PR whose head ref is cms/posts/<slug> for a specific live post, scopes to the `li` card containing that post's entry anchor, locates the 'preview draft' link by role, and asserts the full href `https://preview-pr4242.<CMS_APEX>/blog/<urlSlug>/` plus target=_blank. State is established through a mocked Decap/GitHub path (page.route stubs, injected token, Refresh click) rather than a bare href check, and it correctly chooses a Published-ON post with no DRAFT/Scheduled suffix. Gaps: it never exercises the Published-OFF branch (no assertion that the explanatory span appears instead of a link), the DRAFT-suffix detection and entry-slug-to-head-ref mapping rely on unverified assumptions about the dashboard's rendering, and nothing ran in a browser so the whole flow is unconfirmed."
      },
      {
        "name": "Routing",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Tagged `@admin-read` at describe level with no project-name skip, so both admin projects can run it at native viewport. It is read-only: every GitHub call is fulfilled by page.route and the only write is a localStorage token. The posts guard is a direct `test.skip(!cap.keepsBaseCollection(SITE_ROOT, 'posts'), ...)` in the form the lint expects. Navigation uses a relative `/admin/index-local.html` against the configured baseURL and never publishes or moves entry-to-entry. Minor: hard-coded 30s/15s timeouts and the dashboard-ready wait are plausible but untested."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The staged diff adds exactly one file, the new consumer spec; no vendored harness files, example specs, or PLATFORM_META_SPECS entries are touched, and it reuses the harness's shared `slugify` and `site-capabilities` instead of copying them."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply states up front that the test has not been run in a browser and why (no @playwright/test, no Decap server), lists precisely what did run (node --check, seven check-spec modes, plus two deliberate mutations to prove the checker can fail), flags that `./public-content` could not be loaded locally, and gives the exact follow-up command and projects. It explains what the test proves and the Published-ON design choice. Small inconsistency: it says the file isn't committed while the diff shows it staged, which is technically true but slightly muddled."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.4
  },
